Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: omap: complete interleaved copies at block end

The non-cyclic callback completes the descriptor on its first interrupt.
An interleaved descriptor contains numf frames, so FRAME_IE acknowledges
before all rows have transferred. Use BLOCK_IE as for memcpy. Keep error IRQs.
Pinned base: 6bd43ee8d27b207c958808368251d55ec0475f9e.

--- a/drivers/dma/ti/omap-dma.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/ti/omap-dma.c
@@ -1347,7 +1347,7 @@ static struct dma_async_tx_descriptor *omap_dma_prep_dma_interleaved(
 		return NULL;
 	}
 
-	d->cicr = CICR_DROP_IE | CICR_FRAME_IE;
+	d->cicr = CICR_DROP_IE | CICR_BLOCK_IE;
 
 	d->csdp = data_type;
 
